  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Let $4\\sin x-3\\cos x=A\\sin(x-\\alpha)$, where $A>0$ and $0^\\circ\\leq\\alpha<360^\\circ$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p27-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $A\\cos\\alpha=4$ and $A\\sin\\alpha=3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A\\cos\\alpha=4$ and $A\\sin\\alpha=3$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}A\\sin(x-\\alpha)&=A\\sin x\\cos\\alpha-A\\cos x\\sin\\alpha\\end{aligned}$$\nComparing coefficients of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$:\n$$\\begin{aligned}A\\cos\\alpha&=4\\\\A\\sin\\alpha&=3\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $A=5$ and $\\alpha=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac34\\right)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=5$, $\\alpha=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\dfrac34\\right)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}A^2\\cos^2\\alpha+A^2\\sin^2\\alpha&=4^2+3^2\\\\A^2&=25\\\\A&=5\\qquad(A>0)\\end{aligned}$$\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\tan\\alpha&=\\frac{A\\sin\\alpha}{A\\cos\\alpha}\\\\\\tan\\alpha&=\\frac34\\end{aligned}$$\nBoth $\\sin\\alpha$ and $\\cos\\alpha$ are positive, so $\\alpha$ is in quadrant I.\n$$\\alpha=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac34\\right)$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence solve the equation $4\\sin x-3\\cos x=5$, for $0^\\circ\\leq x\\leq360^\\circ$.\nGive the solution(s) correct to the nearest minute.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\approx126^\\circ52'$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}5\\sin(x-\\alpha)&=5\\\\\\sin(x-\\alpha)&=1\\end{aligned}$$\nThe transformed domain is $-\\alpha\\leq x-\\alpha\\leq360^\\circ-\\alpha$, so the only admissible value is $x-\\alpha=90^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}x-\\alpha&=90^\\circ\\\\x&=90^\\circ+\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac34\\right)\\\\x&\\approx126^\\circ52'\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      }
    ]
  },
